course: dictionary
lesson: 7407
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many English words have more than one meaning. The word point is a good example. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «In the morning the shadows point west» means the shadows show a direction, like a finger does.
explain: Try the meanings in the sentence. If «The point of the pencil broke» is the sentence, point cannot mean a score, because a pencil does not score. It means the sharp end. Always ask: does this meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Some meanings are used in special subjects. In maths, a point can be a dot on a graph, or the decimal point in 3.5, which we read as «three point five». In science, boiling point and freezing point are temperatures. In everyday talk, «What is the point?» asks for the main reason.
fact: A word can have several meanings, and context shows you which one is meant.
fact: Point can mean a score in a game, a very small dot or exact place, the sharp end of something, the main idea, or to show with your finger.
fact: In the number 3.5, the dot is a decimal point, and we say «three point five».
fact: «In the morning the Sun is in the east, so shadows point west.» Here point means lie or show in a direction.
fact: Boiling point and freezing point are temperatures, so the word point can name an exact place on a scale.
exercise: «In the morning the Sun is in the east, so shadows point west.» What does point mean here? | A score in a game | A dot in a number | The sharp end of a pencil | *To show a direction
exercise: Mia scored three points in the game. What is a point here? | The sharp end of something | The main idea | *A score in a game | A very small dot
exercise: Dad says, «Check your pocket, Sherlock.» What does it mean when a clue points the other way? | It is very large | It is written in pencil | *It shows a different direction | It is a score in a game
test: In the number 3.5, what is the dot called? | A main idea | *A decimal point | A sharp point | A score
test: «What is the point?» means what? | *What is the main reason | Which score won the game | Show me with your finger | Where is the dot
exam: «The point of the pencil broke.» What is point? | A score in a game | A dot on a line | The main reason | *The sharp end
